## Build Cycle Complete

**Project:** todo-cli — Python CLI todo manager with SQLite storage, priorities, due dates, and colored terminal output

**Result: SUCCESS**

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Composite eval | 0.99 |
| Tests | 77 passing |
| Coverage | 94% |
| Lint (ruff) | Clean |
| Type check (mypy) | Clean |
| PR | [#3](https://github.com/mihirathale98/e2e-iter-todo/pull/3) (draft, targeting main) |

**Stack:** `typer[all]` (sole production dependency) + sqlite3 stdlib + datetime stdlib + Rich (bundled)

**What was built:**
- 5 CLI commands: `todo add`, `todo list`, `todo complete`, `todo delete`, `todo show`
- SQLite database with CHECK constraints and parameterized queries
- Rich-colored tables with priority highlighting (high=red, medium=yellow, low=green)
- Natural language date parsing (today, tomorrow, +Nd, +Nw, YYYY-MM-DD)
- `--no-color`, `--format json`, `NO_COLOR` env var support
- Comprehensive test suite across 5 test modules
- Eval harness, CLAUDE.md, factory.md for factory loop

**Deferred:** PyPI publishing, Homebrew, recurring tasks, timezone support, tags, cloud sync, FTS5, task editing, advanced filtering — all require human intervention or are post-MVP scope.
